<header class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="page-kicker">About Adrian</p><h1>I build companies, software and assets I want to own for a long time.</h1><p class="page-lede">No reinvention story. Just a clearer view of the kind of work, leverage and responsibility I want.</p></div></header>
<section class="section"><div class="shell about-split">
  <div class="portrait-wrap"><img src="/assets/images/adrianching.jpg" alt="Portrait of Adrian Ching" width="1500" height="1500"></div>
  <div class="content-body"><p class="section-index">The short version</p><h2 class="section-title">Builder first. Owner always.</h2><p>I founded Upstack Studio in 2017 and spent years building custom web and mobile software with business owners. The work taught me how companies make decisions, where software projects go wrong and why technical capability is never the same as commercial judgment.</p><p>Eventually, I shut the agency down rather than keep optimizing a model I no longer wanted to build. It was a deliberate decision about direction.</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section section-soft"><div class="shell">
  <div class="content-grid"><h2>What changed</h2><div class="content-body"><h3>AI changed the economics of building software.</h3><p>Software is becoming faster and cheaper to create. That raises the value of knowing what should exist, what should not and where a business has a defensible advantage.</p><p>It also changed how I think companies will operate: smaller teams, better leverage and much more pressure on the quality of decisions.</p></div></div>
  <div class="content-grid" id="what-im-building"><h2>What I’m building</h2><div class="content-body"><h3>Second Team is the primary company.</h3><p>It is my venture-scale bet and the majority of my working time goes there. I will share the thinking and the journey without exposing unreleased product IP.</p><h3>Adrian Ching is the long-term portfolio.</h3><p>Alongside it, I am building a body of writing, media, software products and other high-margin digital assets. The goal is not a collection of side projects. It is a portfolio of useful things I own, compound and improve over time.</p></div></div>
  <div class="content-grid"><h2>Selective advisory</h2><div class="content-body"><h3>Experience is useful when applied at the right point.</h3><p>I continue to advise a small number of founders where my judgment can create disproportionate value — usually before a consequential AI or software investment, not during day-to-day execution.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work-with-me/">See how I work with founders</a></div></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section section-dark"><div class="shell thinking-grid"><div><p class="section-index">What I write about</p><h2 class="section-title">The work behind the work.</h2></div><div><p class="section-lede">AI and business growth. Building Second Team. Software as a business decision. Founder and operator lessons without the retrospective mythology.</p><div class="actions" style="margin-top:2rem"><a class="button" href="/blog/">Read the writing</a><a class="text-link" href="/newsletter/">Join the newsletter</a></div></div></div></section>
